From e7c794f498f33dc605ca8eff1c78c31e36c9ac56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangtianwen07 <10508155+wangtianwen07@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:18:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: opt-in compact committed prompt snapshots

At a committed mark, save the active FP32 KDA bank for each layer and
omit the projection/replay scratch. Restore with the saved per-layer cur
bits. Keep the live layout, arithmetic and default snapshot path intact.

TF_GLM_SNAPSHOT_FORMAT=committed is agreed in the rank fingerprint and
recorded on each in-memory snapshot. Limit this release to unsharded TP2;
reject disk learning before opening and at disk-image entry points.

This is an independent implementation on the recipe's 121-patch main.
PR #42 separately ports upstream's live-half snapshots (#2181); the
additional scope here is replay scratch omission and mixed-layer parity.
The shared-page store from #42 is not part of this patch.

Host validation: 6 committed-snapshot/configuration tests and 9 disk-open
tests pass, including GLM environment-based TP2 admission. The earlier owner comparison was 22/26 on
both base and candidate, with the same four failures; this revision
changes only native admission and its test. Native CUDA sm_121 builds with Zig 0.17.0.
